WEBVTT

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.530
I hear you've submitted a thirteenth 
article to the Zodiac Precepts.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:16.780
Yes.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.540
Soon...

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.400
Soon, I will be able to destroy the cat.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.460
I'm almost there...

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.800
Cat and rat...

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.550
The connection they share 
is one that nobody can undo.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.400
But...

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.700
<b>ETOTAMA</b>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.740
<b>A Long, Serpentine Fate</b>

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.070
Where should we go next? 
What should we buy?

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:35.070
If we drag our feet, the day will 
be over before we know it!

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.760
You're in an awfully good mood.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.010
Well, yeah! I learned a 
lethal new technique!

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.930
I'm getting so much stronger, 
my own potential frightens me!

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.930
<b>Neko Masshiguran</b>

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.180
Oh?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.890
Hey, Shar-tan! What are you up to?

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.900
What was that? I don't get it.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.090
You're into gardening, Shar-tan?

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.760
No. It's food for this little one.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.120
"Little one"?

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.770
Yes, this little one.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.540
I have to feed it poison regularly.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.580
But that's just a hair ornament, isn't it?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.990
Wait! So is this a poisonous plant?!

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.370
No, that's a bay laure—

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.040
It's bitter! I'm dying! I'm dying!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.900
That was a joke.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.630
Which part was the joke?!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.390
This isn't poisonous. It's a bay 
laurel to use for cooking.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.550
Oh!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.760
So this snake is just a fake, too, right?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.060
Chomp

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.390
Ow!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.390
Be careful.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.730
Too late for that!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.940
Hiss

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.150
This really is a venomous snake.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:36.820
Seriously?!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.230
What?

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.240
Hey! Why am I turning to stone?!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.300
W-Wait! Takeru, do somethi—

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:47.090
Oh, dear.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.490
Nya-tan! Nya-tan!

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.660
What do we do?!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.610
She needs the antidote, 
or she'll be like that forever.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:54.250
No way...

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.460
Where is the antidote?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.310
Let us embark on a journey, then.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.280
Pardon?

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.220
A journey to obtain the antidote.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.500
Wh-What is...

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.130
It's the snake train.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.440
Snake... It's exactly what it looks like.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.190
Now, let's go.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.370
A-All right.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.900
What is this place?

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.630
You're better off not knowing the details.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.220
For a human like you, 
it's quite serpentine logic.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.690
That was a pun using "serpent," 
as in a snake—

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.100
Yeah, you don't have to explain. I got it.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:45.840
I see.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.380
So this goes to a place where we can find

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.930
the antidote to return Nya-tan to normal?

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.880
It might be there, and it might not be.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:54.730
It might not?!

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.850
Just kidding.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:56.910
Which is it?!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:58.990
Look there.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.190
That's the Shrine of the Characters.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:02.950
Huh?

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.070
Shrine of the 
Characters

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.050
We've arrived.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.790
And the antidote is here?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.800
Since we're here, 
let's do some sightseeing.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.430
Look. There's something over there.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:23.000
What's that?

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.570
Now, I'll explain.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.600
What?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.690
Chu-tan.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.810
She is a very scrupulous Eto-shin who 
addresses all things with sincerity.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:44.120
Her favorite food is a product 
stumbled upon around 4,000 BC

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.530
when cow milk stored in a bag made from

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.460
a sheep's stomach hardened due 
to the work of enzymes—

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.590
Cheese, right?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.950
She protects the southern Kanto region.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:53.620
<b>Rat</b>

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:55.870
Next is

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:56.790
<b>Ox</b>

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.620
Mo-tan.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.040
She is a pervert.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.320
She's actually a vegetarian.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.920
No way! Never expected that!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.150
She protects the Tokai region.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:07.840
<b>Ox</b>

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.890
Shima-tan has muscles ideal 
for hand-to-hand combat,

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.720
<b>Tiger</b>

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.850
so she's on the heavy side.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.840
Uh, is it okay to say that?

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.310
Her favorite things are liquor, snacks,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.870
and the plate the snacks were on.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.290
She likes the plate?!

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.620
So that's why she took my—

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.110
She protects the Kinki region.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.070
<b>Tiger</b>

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:30.520
Usa-tan is ten kilograms 
lighter than Shima-tan.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.120
Again, you shouldn't say that...

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.100
She protects Hokuriku.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:35.580
<b>Rabbit</b>

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.460
Dora-tan is an adequate C-cup.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.080
Hey!

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.090
She protects the Tosan region.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.590
<b>Dragon</b>

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.590
And when I say C-cup, I mean

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.970
the difference between the top and under—

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.740
Next, please!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.340
I protect the Chugoku region.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:53.830
That's it?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.260
You should learn many things 
about me on this journey.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:57.850
<b>Snake</b>

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.850
Uma-tan is haunted by the 
unpleasant sound of her name.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.550
Rat, ox, tiger, rabbit,

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.710
dragon, snake... snake...

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.110
Oh, come on. Remember her.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.700
<b>Horse</b>

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.700
She protects the Kyushu region.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:14.530
Mei-tan's greatest concern 
is her yearly shearing.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.370
Shearing?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.750
Every hair on her body is shaved off.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.250
Please don't lie.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.710
<b>Sheep</b>

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.710
She protects Hokkaido.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.410
Can we get to searching for 
Nya-tan's antidote soon?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.240
Key-tan protects northern Kanto,  
Piyo-tan protects Tohoku,

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.970
Inu-tan protects Shikoku,  
and Uri-tan protects Okinawa.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.070
Thanks for consolidating those.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.470
You're welcome.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.450
When I see it this way,

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.510
I can tell the zodiac really 
does protect all of Japan.

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:41.480
Exactly.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.700
That's why we can't lose 
even one of the twelve.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.390
It looks like the antidote isn't here.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.490
We haven't even looked for it...

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.240
Oh, dear. We need to hurry back, 
or the curator will appoint us.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.240
Okay, okay. Let's get going.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.150
That was a close one.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:06.020
Um, this <i>is</i> a journey to

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.750
get the antidote to fix Nya-tan, right?

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:12.010
Yes. It's not a recap 
episode, by any means.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.370
Recap... episode?

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.720
The next stop is the Shrine 
of the ETM12 Setting.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:21.300
Shrine of the ETM12 Setting.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.590
Don't touch this reflective water.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.610
Why not?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.120
The water is difficult to animate.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.840
They can't use as many 
cels in a recap episode.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:40.870
I'm sorry. I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:44.840
I'm going to give you a review 
of what the ETM12 is.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:50.670
<b>Zodiac Precepts</b>

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.920
The ETM12 is carried out

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.660
according to the Zodiac Precepts.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.170
Zodiac Precepts?

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.670
Twelve rules established by the gods.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.060
<b>Dragon</b>

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.890
The Eto-shin Selection Festival, 
held once every sixty years,

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.390
where Eto-musume can attain the rank 
of Eto-shin with their own fists...

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.100
That's the ETM12!

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.940
For Nya-tan to become an Eto-shin,

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.980
she must defeat all twelve Eto-shin in 
battle while the ETM12 is in progress

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:15.650
and obtain all of their Sol/Lull Seals.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.550
If she loses her Sol/Lull Seal,

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.830
<b>Cat</b>

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.410
she can't participate in the ETM12, right?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:29.090
Correct. Nor can she transform 
into Pretty Mode anymore.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.460
Etotama! Sol/Lull Charge!

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:30.960
<b>Cat</b>

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.750
With stuff like this,

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.570
they're usually larger and tougher-looking 
after they transform, right?

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.720
So why do they get smaller?

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.890
It's a result of them being condensed.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.970
Condensed?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.140
Sol/Lull from humans collects in

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.220
our Etotama, our souls,

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.610
and converted into our battle power.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.520
It's when we're the most 
tightly-packed with power.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.260
Sounds kinda like 100% 
juice from concentrate.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.960
By the way, there are

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:02.860
108 Eto-musume participating 
in the ETM12, right?

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:03.830
That's right.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:07.040
I've never met any other than Nya-tan.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.330
All the other Eto-musume

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:12.530
were defeated by Chu-tan.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.670
Chu-tan is that strong?

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.830
Since the ETM12 of 2,000 years ago,

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:23.010
Chu-tan has been the most powerful, 
and the leader of the Eto-shin.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.040
Wasn't the ETM12 of 2,000 years ago...

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.350
It's true that the ETM12 of

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.560
2,000 years ago was a footrace.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.740
And the twelve Zodiac gods chosen 
then were the current twelve.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.930
But that means the cat should hate the rat.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.570
Why does Chu-tan hate Nya-tan?

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.180
The connection between the cat and rat is

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:47.710
a complex, elaborate tangle.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.210
If we tried to undo it by force, 
they would surely be torn apart and die.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.000
Is there something you know, Shar-tan?

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.210
Well,

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.530
I might know, or I might not know.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.930
Oh, it's that time already?

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.650
Time to head for the next shrine.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:10.020
<b>[Zodiac Precepts ~Article 7: "Continuance"]  
If an Eto-shin loses a Sol/Lull Seal battle, 
her Sol/Lull Seal will be transferred to the 
Eto-musume who defeated her. 
The Eto-shin may continue to participate 
in the ETM12 with a new Sol/Lull Seal.</b>

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:14.980
<b>[Zodiac Precepts ~Article 8: "Revocation"]  
An Eto-musume who loses a Sol/Lull Seal battle 
against an Eto-shin will lose her own Sol/Lull Seal, 
and her right to participate in the current ETM12 will be revoked.</b>

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.100
Incidentally, how do you...

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.160
How do you feel about Nya-tan?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:25.990
Huh?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.970
Actually,

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:32.250
Shima-tan and Uri-tan both asked 
me the same thing recently.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.900
When I first met her, 
I had no idea what to do, but...

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:36.920
It seems...

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:41.640
That you are not so opposed 
to a recap episode anymore.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:42.760
What do you mean?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:45.560
You just gave me a line that will

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.920
let us transition smoothly 
into a flashback scene.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.420
Though, we already threw in a 
few flashback scenes earlier.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.020
You're kidding!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.660
You understand well how this should flow.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.070
You're very clever.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:01.520
<i>The next stop is the Shrine of 
Reviewing the Story Thus Far.</i>

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.170
We can stay on the train 
from this point on.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:04.780
<i>Shrine of Reviewing the Story Thus Far.</i>

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:04.780
Huh?

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.400
The snake train is about to molt.

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.150
Molt?!

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.510
Just kidding.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:10.540
This is tiring...

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.880
Shrine of Reviewing
 the Story Thus Far

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.420
Meow.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.420
Did that excite you?

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.680
Did that lick excite you?

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:30.940
Why?!

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:34.940
How are you not excited after a run-in 
with a lucky licking situation like that?!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:35.690
Hmm...

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.060
I see... So this is a lucky situation, huh?

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:38.880
Seriously?

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.640
I don't really get it, but sorry 
I didn't meet your expectations.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:42.440
Depressing!

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:45.490
Meow?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.740
Meow! Onii-chan, you pervert!

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:54.250
Oh, Takeru-han! Do you feel better?

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.880
Where are you going?

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.710
To buy food...

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.900
and scout around.

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:05.120
Add indecent exposure to the charges.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.720
Fidget

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.720
I wish I could jump into a hole!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.440
Here.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.350
<b>Hole</b>

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:10.350
Seriously?!

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:14.600
Pleased to meet you. I'm Uri-tan.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:17.600
So I might as well ask... 
Where'd you come from?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.110
From this hole.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.110
<b>Hole</b>

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.110
I should've known...

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.690
Where does that hole lead to?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.820
The world of the gods.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:24.570
Gods?!

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.310
Sometimes.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:26.610
What do you mean, sometimes?

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.490
Fire!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.830
I might as well ask...

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.490
You know all these people, right?

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:36.590
Yep, yep.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.630
Nya-tan can't help that. She's got amnesia.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:43.330
She's forgotten a lot of important things.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:44.810
Poor girl...

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.140
Everyone working hard?

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:52.030
Huh? What are the Eto-shin doing here?

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.930
They all work at this café.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:55.810
They work?

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.690
Isn't Sol/Lull all they need?

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.430
Sol/Lull and money are 
two different things.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.480
The more money you have, the better.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.920
It never gets in the way.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.390
Right, Shar-tan?

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:07.360
Yes.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.820
She's playing the stock market!

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.300
For me, it's a piece of cake.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.500
You're still dealing in stocks?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.110
Yes.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.790
That seems difficult.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.830
Even without doing anything extraordinary,

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:22.570
it's possible to gain 
extraordinary results.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.070
As long as you follow the basic rules.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.350
Huh...

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.500
So this is where you are.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:34.780
Chu-tan!

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:35.850
Chu-tan?

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.640
She's the rat Eto-shin.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.900
I will only destroy the cat clan.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.040
If it gets dangerous, surrender right away.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.400
Got that, idiot student?

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:48.740
What are you trying to do?

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.820
I'm going to intervene in the battle.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.160
Intervene?!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:55.370
Even if you're an Eto-shin, doin' 
somethin' that crazy will mess you up!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.320
Still!

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.960
Nya-tan is my friend.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.750
I can't just keep watching this!

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.880
You will exist no more!

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:15.220
Uri-tan!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.020
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.230
Here's the cake you ordered, yep, yep.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.560
"Yep, yep"?

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.110
Reincarnated?

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.870
Yes. Even if we die,

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:31.040
we reincarnate after a 
certain amount of time.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.560
What kind of system is that?

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.580
Exactly that kind of system, apparently.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.450
It's the UTC,

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.080
Usa-tan Company's helicopter!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.370
Usa-tan Company?

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.710
Forgive my delayed introduction.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:50.880
<b>Usa-tan Company, CEO 
Usa-tan Productions, Producer 
Usa-tan Moving Center, Inc., Representative 
Usa-tan Visual Effects, Inc., Managing Director 
Usa-tan Books, Inc., Managing Director 
UTC Electronics, President 
UTC Foods, Inc., Representative Director</b>

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.380
I'm the CEO of Usa-tan Company,

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.880
producer of Usa-tan Productions, 
and much more.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.760
Is Usa-tan Company really that amazing?

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.020
Oh, didn't you notice?

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.060
Notice what?

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.640
All of these belong to the Usa-tan Group.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.020
<b>All There Is to Know About Sesame Oil</b>

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:05.220
Huh?! That's what "UTC" was?

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:07.590
But as long as I follow the basic rules,

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.130
it may be a good time to sell.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:11.650
You own UTC stock?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.270
I just sold it.

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:14.160
Seriously?!

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.620
Takeru!

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.830
What is this?!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.460
What is this?!

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:36.300
What is that?!

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.020
What is this chaos?!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.810
I am all in one, and one in all.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.150
I reign over all realms, godly and mortal.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:49.020
Eh? What? All in one? All realms?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.020
I am the true divine cold virus!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.950
Oh, right! You're the one I've heard of!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.780
The one causing havoc everywhere right now,

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.700
the divine cold virus!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.850
Wait! Cut it out already!

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.830
I'm sorry!

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.920
A kick-the-can battle.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:21.110
At this rate, Chu-tan really will beat you!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.140
Hurry up and surrender, Nya-tan.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:27.320
Come with me to train and 
start over from scratch!

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.480
No!

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:37.200
Takeru produces such amazing

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.690
Sol/Lull because he is who he is!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.640
I've forgotten a lot of things.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:44.410
I don't even remember why I wanted to

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.040
join the zodiac in the first place, but—

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.390
Wh-When I'm with Takeru,

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.420
sesame oil tastes better,

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.260
hot baths feel nicer,

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.970
and breakfast and trips out of the 
house and everything else is fun!

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.190
It's because Takeru is with me

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:06.190
that I can give all I've got to making my 
dream of joining the zodiac come true!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.320
He's not a battery!

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.970
I can believe that because he's Takeru!

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.530
<b>Cat</b>

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.610
Nya-tan's gotten stronger, huh?

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.600
You've been watching her, I see.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.590
I believe Nya-tan trusts you.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.360
Trusts me? You think so?

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:02.810
By becoming involved with a human like you,

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.120
Nya-tan changed.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.870
You changed, as well.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:11.090
Lives change by becoming 
involved with other lives.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.310
But those changes

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:16.380
may not always be for the better.

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:20.430
Looks like we're done with the review.

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:21.240
Yes.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.920
Um... And the antidote...?

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:25.210
It wasn't here, it seems.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:27.200
You didn't even look for it, did you?

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.140
Let's search there next.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.790
What is this?

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.370
This is Nya-tan's shrine.

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:44.270
What? This place?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:48.330
It must be because her soul 
hasn't completely regenerated.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:50.660
Oh?

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.420
Sol/Lull? No, it's not...

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.420
Nya-tan's... memories?

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.420
What does this mean?

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.500
If we take these back to Nya-tan,

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.110
will she remember more?

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.880
Why would you make her remember?

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.280
Something sad may have happened.

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:11.870
Do you want to have a part in 
the things she's sealed away?

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.580
I'm not a god or an Eto-musume,

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.580
so maybe it's strange for me to say...

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.440
But I'm the one able to support 
Nya-tan the most right now,

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.450
aren't I?

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:26.920
When on a journey, everyone 
experiences meetings,

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.890
partings, and lessons.

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:32.160
And they halt the train at the stop 
they've found just for themselves.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.460
I only wanted to see what stop 
you would find, Takeru.

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:41.130
I want to see all of Nya-tan's 
memories here before I go back.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.470
That's not possible.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:45.010
This place will soon disappear.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:45.900
What?

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:53.600
Shar-tan's special curry is done.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.490
It's finally finished.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:00.230
Wow. Looks tasty.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.490
This curry is the antidote.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.330
You're kidding me!

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.300
It needs plenty of time to cook 
in order to undo petrification.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:10.200
Oh... The bay leaves you 
grew are in it, too.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.990
They should actually be removed 
before the roux goes in.

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:15.640
Wait, you're not saying this whole journey

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:19.190
was to kill time while the 
curry cooked, are you?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.110
That may be, or it may not be.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:29.470
Stupid

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.320
Uh-oh!

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.790
Hey, hurry up!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.080
Run!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.470
Meat

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:30.020
Let's go!

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:30.880
Cruel.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.320
Oh, right.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.730
<b>Snake</b>

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.040
Here.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.290
Your Sol/Lull Seal?

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:39.600
A commemorative stamp.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.240
Eat up.

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:47.990
Hot! That's hot!

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:51.280
It burned my tongue...

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:52.110
Oh, good... You're back.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:53.610
What happened?

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.490
Look, Shar-tan gave me her Sol/Lull Seal.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:55.690
<i>Takeru...</i>

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:59.110
<i>If anyone can touch the</i>

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:58.220
Seriously?! Why?!

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:01.650
Lucky! Give it to me, Takeru!

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:01.650
<i>cat and rat's relationship, perhaps it's you...</i>

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.640
Hey, calm down a little. And no.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.010
Don't say that!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:46.820
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:37.900
The fortune for those of you born 
in the year of the snake...

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.940
Oh. There isn't one, really.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:40.470
Huh?

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:42.900
Your lucky item is a molted snakeskin.

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:44.540
Hang on. I'll take mine off.

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:45.150
Whoa! Wait!

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.820
Just kidding.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:49.010
Next time: An Equestrian Fit for a Cat.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>An Equestrian Fit for a Cat</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>I'm Shar, but I'm not three times faster.</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Snake</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>You Should Watch Again Next Week... For Sure. 
